# This repo ships the workspace *system* only — the rules, commands, skills and
# scripts. Every directory below is tracked, and carries a README explaining
# what belongs in it; the contents stay local, because they describe private
# services and their production incidents.
#
# Note: each rule ignores `dir/*`, not `dir/` — git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so the README would vanish with it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- checkouts --
# Canonical service checkouts, cloned per machine. Full clones of the private
# services, carrying their own .env files and service-account keys.
/repos/*
!/repos/README.md

# Task worktrees for tasks started with --space, created by .claude/scripts/task.sh
# and removed when the task finishes. Every file inside belongs to a service repo.
/spaces/*
!/spaces/README.md

# Which tasks are open on this machine: isolation, branch, and each repo's base.
# Written by task.sh, read through tasklib.sh; see tasklib.sh for the format.
/.claude/state/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- task docs --
# One directory per task - prd.md, plan.md, log.md, testing.md. They narrate real
# bugs and fixes in the private services, so only the README is tracked.
/docs/*
!/docs/README.md

# Release runbooks: commit-level state across the private repos.
/release/*
!/release/README.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- tooling --
# Per-machine Claude Code overrides. settings.json is shared; .local is not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# What skills learned about each repo (.claude/learned/<repo>/<skill>.md): which
# logger a service uses, where it leaks data. They describe the private services,
# so like docs/ only the README is tracked; each machine learns its own via /learn.
/.claude/learned/*
!/.claude/learned/README.md

# Per-machine workspace settings - branch prefix, default base ref. Everyone
# has their own; .env.example is the tracked template. See .claude/scripts/config.sh.
/.env
!/.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- noise --
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

.env
# code-review-graph data - rebuilt from the code on demand by .claude/scripts/graph.sh.
/.code-review-graph/

# MCP servers for this machine's checkouts - graph.sh rewrites it on every build,
# so it names only the services cloned here.
/.mcp.json
